e review window, and the volume time series is bursty (step_03: 62\u2013141 events per 3k bin), with individual members switching on and off entirely \u2014 e.g. 384 is active only in [33806, 37806] and dead thereafter (step_12, step_14), 1116 is active only in [43306, 47306] (step_04\u2013step_08), 946/716/1955 have zero-activity spans (step_21, step_23, step_26). That on/off pattern is exactly what would produce a spurious \"change point\" if one looked at volume or at per-node presence alone.\n\nBut the diagnostic question is whether the *partner set* turns over. It does not. Every group member, in every window in which it is active, contacts the identical fixed pool of 30 nodes {98, 117, 204, 205, 258, 292, 295, 379, 537, 543, 762, 927, 964, 1020, 1045, 1106, 1123, 1155, 1179, 1184, 1247, 1257, 1283, 1294, 1297, 1410, 1460, 1638, 1848, 1950}:\n\n- Early side: 384 in [33806,43806] (step_13), 716 in [33806,38806] (step_30), 948 in [38806,43806] (step_28)\n- Mid: 1121 in [43806,48806] (step_22, same 30 plus one extra, 831), 1116 in [41306,48806] (step_05, same 30 plus 439/1986)\n- Late side: 1304 in [48806,53806] (step_19), 1464 and 1635 in [53806,58806] (step_25, step_31), 1740 in [48806,63806] and [58806,63806] (step_15, step_29)\n\nTaking the most plausible candidate change point (~48806) with the prescribed 5000 half-windows: the \"before\" contact set [43806,48806] is the 30-node pool \u222a {831}, and the \"after\" set [48806,53806] is the same 30-node pool \u2014 Jaccard \u2248 30/31 \u2248 0.97. There is no old set giving way to a new set; the neighbourhood is invariant. The apparent discontinuities are member dormancy/reactivation over a static partner pool, not partner replacement.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_459f9d4b\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [384, 716, 946, 948, 1116, 1121, 1304, 1464, 1572, 1635, 1740, 1955],\n  \"window\": [33806, 63806],\n  \"confidence\": 0.89,\n  \"evidence\": [\n   